```javascript
function debounce(fn, wait) {
  let timeoutId;
  return function (...args) {
    clearTimeout(timeoutId);
    timeoutId = setTimeout(() => fn.apply(this, args), wait);
  };
}
```

This function returns a new version of `fn` that delays its execution until `wait` milliseconds have passed since the last time it was called. Every time the debounced function is invoked, it clears any previously scheduled timeout and sets a new one, ensuring `fn` only runs after the user stops triggering it for the specified duration. This is commonly used to optimize performance

